@startuml

title Correlation Identifier: what a handler does with the id

start
:a message arrives;
if (Nats-Correlation-Id header present?) then (yes)
  if (well formed: 32 hex digits\nor a uuid, bounded length?) then (yes)
    :use it;
  else (no)
    :create a new id;
    :log the rejected value's length,\nnot the value;
  endif
else (no)
  :create a new id;
  :log "no correlation id arrived";
endif
:open a log scope with correlation_id;
note right: every log line of this\nhandling now carries the id
:forward the id on every outbound call\nand every event this work publishes;
:store it with any work that outlives the request;
:echo it on the reply, success or error;
:close the log scope;
stop
@enduml
